at most people do not even know that they have come from a far away land. - Plants have thick fleshy stems with broad simple leaves. - The stems and trunk get a twisted and garnled look when old. - The flowers are borne in huge terminal trusses. They are generally above the foliage. Growing tips: - Plumerias are hardy plants and will grow in a range of soils. - They are well known for their tenacity and ability to grow in poor soils. - Some varieties drop their leaves - especially if not irrigated in winter. - Regular fertilizer application and good soils will make the plants grow better. - Plants require regular pruning to stay in shape. Pruning should be done just after the flower flush is over. - Plumerias grow well in absolutely all kinds of soils. - They can be grown in pots as well as the ground. - Plumerias can go without water for long periods of time. - However regular irrigation in the hot summer growing months will make them bloom better and have a fresher looking crown. - Can be cut back if they are getting too big. - Plants grow and flower well in containers as well. Choose large sizes for optimum growth. - Do not over fertilize as plants will only put out leaves and soft growth. A bit of starvation - makes them flower more.	9353.22	products/product_8925.jpg	72	PlantsMarket	2026-09-24 09:28:49.687984+05:30	2026-09-24 09:28:49.691615+05:30	3214
